      "text": " <think>\nTo find the product of 27 and 88, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. Write down the numbers one below the other, aligning them by their place values:\n   ```\n     27\n   x 88\n   ```\n\n2. Multiply 27 by the ones digit of 88 (which is 8):\n   ```\n     27\n   x  8\n   ----\n     216\n   ```\n\n3. Multiply 27 by the tens digit of 88 (which is 80, or 8 with a zero added at the end):\n   ```\n     27\n   x 80\n   ----\n    2160\n   ```\n\n4. Add the two products together:\n   ```\n     216\n   +2160\n   ----\n    2376\n   ```\n\nSo, the product of 27 and 88 is 2376.\n</think>\n<answer>\n2376\n</answer>",
