      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the math problem of finding the product of 19 and 99, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. This property states that a(b + c) = ab + ac. In this case, we can rewrite 99 as 100 - 1. So, the expression becomes 19(100 - 1). Now, we can distribute the 19 to both terms inside the parentheses: 19(100) - 19(1). This simplifies to 1900 - 19. Finally, we subtract 19 from 1900 to get the answer.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 19 and 99 is 1881.\n</answer>",
