      "text": " <think>\nTo find the product of 39 and 60, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. We can break down the numbers into their factors and then multiply them separately. \n\n39 can be broken down into 30 and 9, and 60 can be broken down into 6 and 10. \n\nSo, we can rewrite the problem as:\n\n(30 + 9) * (6 + 10)\n\nNow, we can use the distributive property to multiply each factor:\n\n(30 * 6) + (30 * 10) + (9 * 6) + (9 * 10)\n\nNow, we can calculate each of these products:\n\n(30 * 6) = 180\n(30 * 10) = 300\n(9 * 6) = 54\n(9 * 10) = 90\n\nFinally, we can add these products together:\n\n180 + 300 + 54 + 90 = 624\n\nSo, the product of 39 and 60 is 624.\n</think>\n<answer>\n624\n</answer>",
