      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the math problem of finding the product of 12 and 17, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the Problem**: The problem asks us to find the result of multiplying 12 by 17. This means we need to add 12 to itself 17 times or add 17 to itself 12 times.\n\n2. **Break Down the Multiplication**: We can break down the multiplication into simpler parts. One way to do this is to use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. We can rewrite 17 as 10 + 7. So, the product of 12 and 17 can be expressed as:\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 17 = 12 \\times (10 + 7)\n   \\]\n\n3. **Apply the Distributive Property**: Using the distributive property, we can distribute the 12 across the sum of 10 and 7:\n   \\[\n   12 \\times (10 + 7) = 12 \\times 10 + 12 \\times 7\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate Each Term**: Now, we calculate each term separately:\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 10 = 120\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   12 \\times 7 = 84\n   \\]\n\n5. **Add the Results**: Finally, we add the results of the two calculations:\n   \\[\n   120 + 84 = 204\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 12 and 17 is \\boxed{204}.",
